        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Clay County, South Dakota\n- People: Henry Clay Sr.\n- Roles: American statesman, lawyer, planter, orator, United States Senator, United States Representative, United States Secretary of State\n\nFacts:\n- Henry Clay Sr. was born on April 12, 1777, and died on June 29, 1852.\n- Henry Clay Sr. was an American lawyer, planter, statesman, and skilled orator.\n- Henry Clay Sr. represented Kentucky in both the United States Senate and the United States House of Representatives.\n- Henry Clay Sr. served as a member of the United States Senate from Kentucky and as United States Secretary of State in the 19th century.\n- Clay County, South Dakota, is named in honor of Henry Clay Sr.",
